    title_en: "Canadian Intelligence Agency Obtains Court Order to Cleanse Two Foreign-Operated Botnets for the First Time",
    summary_en: "The Canadian Security Intelligence Service (CSIS) obtained a federal court order, marking the first time it has used its threat mitigation powers to cleanse infected servers, SOHO routers, and Internet of Things (IoT) devices within Canada, neutralizing two foreign-operated botnets. The court noted that because the cleansing action could constitute computer mischief under the Criminal Code, CSIS was required to obtain judicial authorization. The action targeted the devices themselves, and emphasized that no content would be intercepted or personal identifying information collected. These two botnets utilized a standard relay pattern, hijacking Canadian hardware to allow foreign nations to masquerade as normal connections, thereby probing Canadian critical infrastructure, government, and military networks. The article pointed out that such attacks target poorly maintained equipment, such as decommissioned routers or IoT devices with unupdated firmware, and advised device owners to proactively retire old hardware and strengthen security measures.",
