    title: "Windows 11 低延遲模式（Low Latency Profile）提升舊型電腦體驗：實測 i3-6100 提升啟動與搜尋速度",
    summary: "本文測試了 Windows 11 的「低延遲模式」（Low Latency Profile）功能，該功能旨在透過瞬間提升 CPU 頻率，加速啟動選單、搜尋和動作中心等 Shell 互動。測試對象為一台 2016 年的 Lenovo ThinkCentre M700 mini-PC，搭載 6 代 Intel Core i3-6100 處理器。文章指出，雖然現代處理器有 Turbo Boost，但在 i3-6100 這類無 Turbo Boost 的舊型晶片上，該模式能將 CPU 頻率從閒置的 800MHz 快速提升至其最高定頻 3.7GHz，顯著減少了操作上的感知延遲。使用者可透過安裝 KB5094126 更新後，使用第三方工具 ViVeTool 執行 `vivetool /enable /id:58989092` 來強制啟用此功能。作者提醒，由於 ViVeTool 為第三方工具，建議等待微軟官方推送。此功能在舊硬體上能有效提升使用者體驗，但對 CPU、電池和散熱方面並無負面影響。",
    tags: ["Windows 11", "Low Latency Profile", "i3-6100", "KB5094126", "ThinkCentre M700", "CPU 效能"],
    title_en: "Windows 11 Low Latency Profile Boosts Older Computer Experience: Testing i3-6100 Improves Startup and Search Speed",
    summary_en: "This article tested Windows 11's \"Low Latency Profile\" feature, which aims to accelerate Shell interactions such as the Start menu, search, and Action Center by instantly boosting CPU frequency. The test subject was a 2016 Lenovo ThinkCentre M700 mini-PC equipped with a 6th Gen Intel Core i3-6100 processor. The article points out that while modern processors have Turbo Boost, this mode can rapidly increase the CPU frequency from an idle 800MHz to its maximum fixed frequency of 3.7GHz on older chips like the i3-6100, significantly reducing perceived operational latency. Users can force enable this feature by installing the KB5094126 update and using the third-party tool ViVeTool to execute `vivetool /enable /id:58989092`. The author advises waiting for an official Microsoft push since ViVeTool is a third-party tool. While this feature effectively improves user experience on older hardware, it does not negatively impact the CPU, battery, or cooling.",
    tags_en: ["Windows 11", "Low Latency Profile", "i3-6100", "KB5094126", "ThinkCentre M700", "CPU Performance"],
