    summary_en: "This article discusses multiple feature updates and improvements in Microsoft's New Outlook on Windows 11, aiming to make the user experience closer to the traditional Outlook Classic. Although New Outlook offers several new features, the article points out that it still has flaws in areas such as notification handling and email loading speed, and has not fully replaced Outlook Classic. Key updates include: support for advanced Mail Merge, allowing personalized replacement of fields like names and companies; providing an 'All-accounts view,' enabling users to manage emails from multiple accounts in a single inbox; enhanced folder control, allowing users to select whether to display unread or total item counts; furthermore, it integrates Office files, supports PST file import for calendars and contacts, and adds delegate sharing permissions. These updates are expected to be rolled out gradually from the first half to the second half of 2026. Practically, users are advised to evaluate the functional differences between the new and old versions and wait for improved stability.",
