    id: "20260622-064",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "AI 平台 Dify 爆發「DifyTap」漏洞群，允許攻擊者竊取對話紀錄與敏感文件",
    summary: "資安業者 Zafran 揭露熱門開源 AI 開發平台 Dify 存在四項統稱為「DifyTap」的嚴重漏洞。這些漏洞包括追蹤配置缺陷 (CVE-2026-41947)、Plugin Daemon 路徑遍歷 (CVE-2026-41948)、以及兩項涉及文件預覽與跨用戶存取權限的繞過問題 (CVE-2026-41949、CVE-2026-41950)。攻擊者可藉此建立持續性資料竊取通道，監控企業 AI 聊天對話歷史，或在未經授權下預覽並取得用戶上傳的敏感文件。目前尚未發現實際攻擊案例。官方已針對上述漏洞釋出修補版本，建議用戶儘速更新至最新版，或在特定版本下採用 WAF 規則進行防禦。",
    tags: ["Dify", "DifyTap", "AI 安全", "CVE-2026-41947", "CVE-2026-41948", "資料外洩", "Zafran"],
    title_en: "AI Platform Dify Exposed to 'DifyTap' Vulnerability Cluster, Allowing Attackers to Steal Conversation Records and Sensitive Files",
    summary_en: "Security firm Zafran has disclosed four severe vulnerabilities in the popular open-source AI development platform, Dify, collectively named 'DifyTap'. These vulnerabilities include a tracking configuration flaw (CVE-2026-41947), a Plugin Daemon path traversal issue (CVE-2026-41948), and two bypass issues related to file preview and cross-user access permissions (CVE-2026-41949, CVE-2026-41950). Attackers can exploit these flaws to establish persistent data exfiltration channels, monitor corporate AI chat conversation history, or preview and obtain sensitive files uploaded by users without authorization. No actual attack cases have been discovered yet. The official team has released patched versions for the aforementioned vulnerabilities and advises users to update to the latest version promptly, or implement WAF rules for defense in specific versions.",
    tags_en: ["Dify", "DifyTap", "AI Security", "CVE-2026-41947", "CVE-2026-41948", "Data Leakage", "Zafran"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Dark Reading", url: "https://darkreading.com/application-security/difytap-bugs-wiretap-ai-chat-histories", lang: "EN" }
    ]
