    summary_en: "This article is not a cybersecurity news item, but it discusses the user experience and hardware limitations of Google Chromecast and Google TV Streamers. The author points out that while the Google TV Streamer operates stably, its size is excessive compared to earlier, smaller Dongle designs. Users have encountered issues such as latency and screen stuttering when using core applications like YouTube, suspecting these are due to hardware bottlenecks such as the 2GB memory and processor. Furthermore, the processing overhead of Gemini voice control led the author to abandon its use. The author urges Google to focus on the low-end market, launching a small, low-cost Google TV streamer similar to the Pixel A-series, to provide a more aesthetically pleasing and economically viable option, preventing users from being forced to purchase expensive and bulky models.",
