    title: "特斯拉自動輔助駕駛事故致傷亡：警方調查車禍責任與技術可靠性",
    summary: "本文報導了一起悲劇的車禍事件：一名男子駕駛特斯拉 Model 3，聲稱當時啟用了自動駕駛輔助系統（Autopilot），最終失控將車輛撞向一位德州年長婦人的家中。哈里斯縣警署確認，該男子在事故發生時確實啟用了自動輔助駕駛系統。警方正在調查該自動駕駛功能是否與事故有關，但目前已確認駕駛人未酒醉，並正在協助警方了解 Autopilot 的運作機制。警署指出，該男子未能維持在單一車道行駛，偏離車道並以高速撞擊了住宅。事故造成一位 76 歲的婦人身受重傷，最終不幸身亡。目前，警方和家屬仍在釐清事故的真正責任歸屬，不確定是駕駛人操作失誤，還是車輛自動駕駛系統的技術問題。",
    tags: ["特斯拉", "Tesla", "Autopilot", "自動駕駛", "車禍事故", "AI 安全"],
    title_en: "Tesla Autopilot Accident Causes Fatalities: Police Investigate Liability and Technical Reliability",
    summary_en: "This article reports on a tragic car accident: a man driving a Tesla Model 3, who claimed to have the Autopilot driver-assistance system enabled, lost control and crashed into the home of an elderly woman in Texas. The Harris County Sheriff's Office confirmed that the driver did indeed have the Autopilot system engaged at the time of the incident. Police are investigating whether the automated driving feature played a role in the crash; however, it has been confirmed that the driver was not intoxicated, and he is assisting police in understanding the mechanics of the Autopilot system. The Sheriff's Office noted that the man failed to maintain a single lane, veered off the road, and struck the residence at a high rate of speed. The accident left a 76-year-old woman with severe injuries, which ultimately proved fatal. Currently, authorities and the victim's family are working to determine the true liability, as it remains unclear whether the incident was caused by human error or a technical issue with the vehicle's automated driving system.",
    tags_en: ["Tesla", "Tesla", "Autopilot", "Autonomous Driving", "Car Accident", "AI Safety"],
